  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Existing evidence shows multiprofile avgpool and weighted multimodal fusion are strong, and scvi_n200 gives the best result so far (0.678 accuracy, 0.646 F1) with resnet50, but that is a single multimodal data point and the RNA encoder effect is confounded with fusion. config_005 tests scvi_n200 in the same RNA-only multiprofile avgpool setting as config_002 (pca_n2000, 0.591 accuracy) and config_008 (scgpt, 0.530 accuracy), changing only the RNA encoder. This will clarify whether the learned scvi representation is intrinsically better or mainly beneficial in multimodal fusion, and whether a simpler RNA-only model may be competitive. Under limited budget, this one-factor ablation efficiently reduces uncertainty about an important representation choice before committing further experiments to more complex multimodal extensions."
}

